#21101
Among the Skin Trees~
   The trunks are warm to the touch, and they flinch. Faces push out of the
bark, eyes closed, mouths moving. They are the people the forest has taken,
absorbed into the wood, still alive. They whisper to you to cut them free,
or to cut them down, or to join them.
~
